cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EDGAR-X, please cite the working paper."
title: "EDGAR-X: A Point-in-Time Benchmark for Bankruptcy Prediction from SEC Filings"
abstract: >-
  A point-in-time benchmark for predicting US Chapter 7 or Chapter 11 bankruptcy
  within 365 days of a Form 10-K, in which every input is fixed against that
  filing's EDGAR acceptance timestamp. The panel holds 59,500 Form 10-K
  observations from 2012 to 2024 carrying 437 bankruptcy-positive observations,
  of which 54,351 observations and 408 positive observations are testable under
  rolling temporal evaluation. The repository includes a signed audit of four
  information-set contamination channels and a controlled comparison of filing
  text against financial ratios under a common sparse linear model family.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Upadhyay
    given-names: Bhavya
    email: officiallybhavya@gmail.com
license: MIT
keywords:
  - bankruptcy prediction
  - point-in-time data
  - SEC filings
  - benchmark contamination
  - average precision
  - textual analysis
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-23"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bhavyaupadhyayy/edgar-x-benchmark"
notes: >-
  The version field is the benchmark release version (v1.0.0), which is what
  this repository packages. The accompanying working paper is separately
  versioned and is at v1.2; the two version lines are deliberately
  independent, so that fixing manuscript wording does not imply a new
  benchmark release and vice versa. No DOI has been minted.
